    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jose Caballero** (80.26) and **Corbin Carroll** (79.53) anchor our starting nine as the clear elite plays. **Jose Caballero** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Andrew Abbott, where the combination of the favorable park and the dynamic platoon edge vaults his efficiency well above the baseline. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start; even against a capable arm like Taj Bradley, the \"slow delivery\" metric from the opposition provides the exact catalyst we need to exploit **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s elite speed for stolen base potential. Rounding out the high-efficiency tier, **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Seiya Suzuki** both eclipse the 72-point mark, largely driven by favorable SP skill gaps and park factors that play into their respective profiles.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles today, specifically regarding **Josh Naylor** and **Brice Turang**, who both face tough left-handed starters in Connelly Early and Chris Sale, respectively. Their scores hover in the mid-40s, making them marginal starts, but we are keeping them active to maintain our 5x5 category floor. **Zach McKinstry** was the closest call for the bench; his 42.06 score kept him in the conversation, but he was ultimately relegated to the pine because his negative SP skill modifier against Sean Newcomb made him less efficient than our locked-in starters. **Dalton Rushing** also carries some risk today; while he benefits from favorable wind conditions, his sub-50 efficiency score is a byproduct of a difficult lefty-on-lefty matchup against Trevor Rogers and a bottom-of-the-order assignment.\n\nOwners should exercise caution with the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Alex Freeland**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Cole Young**, and **Kyle Karros**. If these players shift into more aggressive batting order spots, their scores will climb, but any late-scratch or day-off surprises will require immediate roster rotation. We are also tracking the status of **Mickey Moniak**, who remains unavailable on the IL. Ensure that all non-confirmed lineups are re-verified at first pitch to avoid leaving efficiency on the table, particularly for our high-leverage speed threats like **Travis Bazzana**, who relies heavily on his projected lead-off spot to maximize his category contributions.",
